  "body": "Refs #3328. Part of #1448.\n\n## What is missing\n\nPR for #3328 gives Drill, Bore and Thread a start pick and an exit pick as the hole order. The operation page has typed rows (\"First hole X / Y\", \"Last hole X / Y\"). MCP `edit_operation` sets the picks.\n\nThe viewport pick is not there. The design of #3324 (section 5) says: the viewport pick snaps to a hole for `PickCapability::HoleOrder`. Today `crates/ui/src/start_exit_pick.rs` takes a click only for the 2D Contour (`collecting`, `take`, `marks`).\n\n## Expected\n\n- The Start point and Exit point groups of Drill, Bore and Thread have a Pick button, as the 2D Contour has.\n- A click in the viewport snaps to the nearest hole of the operation. It writes the centre of that hole into the draft.\n- A click that is on no hole of the operation writes nothing. The status line says so by name.\n- The marks of the two picks show on the holes while the tab is open.\n- Apply or Generate commits the draft through `EditOperationParams`.\n\n## Seams\n\n- `crates/ui/src/start_exit_pick.rs`: `collecting`, `take`, `marks`.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/start_exit_rows.rs`: `hole_order_groups`.\n- `camcraft_motion::drilling::hole_order` has the rule for \"a pick is on a hole\".\n\n## Done means\n\n- A UI test clicks a hole and reads the centre of the hole in the draft.\n- A UI test clicks off every hole and reads the refusal in the status line.\n- Undo restores the earlier pick.\n",
